# scripts/js_number_lint.py: every 64-bit integer (u64, i64, u128, i128,
# usize, isize) that reaches the window typed as a number, with why it stays
# below 2^53, where the window's numbers (f64) stop being exact. AJ-E1612
# (045c97acb): the notices' version, a wrapping sum plus a hash, lost its
# last bits there and the rail went stale.
# Format: <Type.field | command name(arg) | command name->>  # why
# A value bounded by code, not by what it is, names the function that
# bounds it: [bound: <file>::<fn>]; that function must keep masking with a
# `(1 << 53) - 1` const. A hash, random id, nanosecond time or wrapping sum
# never goes here unbounded: mask it, or send it as a string.
